From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] proximity: allow udev to select the raw channel

The SX9360 grip sensor exposes two proximity channels, a reference
(in_proximity0_raw) and the main electrode (in_proximity1_raw). The
driver's first channel is the reference, which does not react to a hand,
so the proxy would read the wrong one. Let a udev rule name the raw
attribute to read, and keep the existing in_proximity/in_proximity0
lookup as the fallback for other drivers.
---
--- a/src/drv-iio-poll-proximity.c
+++ b/src/drv-iio-poll-proximity.c
@@ -85,8 +85,22 @@
 		"in_proximity",
 		"in_proximity0"
 	};
+	const char *attr_name;
 	guint i;
 
+	/* Some drivers expose several channels and the useful one is not the
+	 * first (the SX9360's channel 0 is the reference electrode). Let udev
+	 * name the attribute to read. */
+	attr_name = g_udev_device_get_property (device, "PROXIMITY_RAW_ATTR");
+	if (attr_name) {
+		g_autofree char *path = NULL;
+
+		path = g_strdup_printf ("%s/%s", g_udev_device_get_sysfs_path (device),
+					attr_name);
+		if (g_file_test (path, G_FILE_TEST_EXISTS))
+			return g_strdup (attr_name);
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < G_N_ELEMENTS (channels); i++) {
 		g_autofree char *path = NULL, *attr = NULL;
 		gboolean exists = FALSE;
